! jb_af1c "PAU GATES ROUTINE", the SHF0 block, p.180 and p.199
! (octal 022367.00-022400.00).  The routine's own header: "THIS ROUTINE
! TESTS THE SEVERAL GATES AND REGISTERS LOCATED IN PANELS A1, A2, A3,
! A4 AND B1 OF FRAME 25, AND ALL OF FRAMES 26 AND 27.  ONLY THE
! FRACTION OPERATIONS ARE CHECKED ... INCLUDED IN THE TESTS FOR THE
! GATES ARE TESTS OF THE F REGISTER AND SHIFT CONTROL REGISTER."
!
! WHY THIS BLOCK AND NOT THE WHOLE ROUTINE.  Everything transcribed so
! far -- every F2xx block -- is a straight line over a constant pool.
! This is the first LOOP: LX loads an index register from a control
! word, the operands are indexed (WRDA($X1), WRDB($X1)), and CBR+
! counts and branches and refills.  It exercises the index machinery
! and the VFL data path together, which nothing in the suite does, and
! it does it over a table rather than a hand-picked pair.  SHF0 is the
! smallest block of the routine that has all of that, and it is
! self-contained for a reason worth noticing: the shift is by ZERO, so
! the expected values ARE the input tables and no separate result
! table is needed.  Every other block of the routine (SHFR1-3,
! SHFL1-3, ...) shifts by a real amount and needs its own WRDAR/WRDBR
! or WRDAL/WRDBL pair.
!
! WHAT IT CHECKS.  Each iteration loads WRDA[i] into the accumulator's
! left word (64 bits at offset 64 = IBM 0-63), adds WRDB[i] into the
! right word (64 bits at offset 0 = IBM 64-127), shifts the fraction
! by zero, and then compares IBM 12-63 against WRDA's own bits 12-63
! and IBM 64-107 against WRDB's bits 0-43.  A shift of zero must leave
! both halves exactly as they were.  The error exits on p.198 name the
! three ways it can go wrong: "ZERO SHIFT HI 52 BITS", "ZERO SHIFT LOW
! 44 BITS" and "ZERO PRE SHIFT DECODING".
!
! WHAT IT DOES NOT CHECK, recorded so the next reader does not repeat
! my mistake: it never branches on LC.  Its only indicator branches are
! the two BZB on $RZ from the CT compares.  A note in the SHF arm once
! claimed this block would close the left-shift-with-LC-off coverage
! gap; it cannot, and that note has been retracted.
!
! THIS BLOCK CANNOT TELL WHETHER ITS OWN LOOP RAN, and the suite entry
! carries two extra assertions because of it.  Measured by injection:
! make the 24-bit VFL effective address ignore its index register
! entirely, or make CBR never take its branch so the loop runs once
! instead of twice, and in BOTH cases the block reports no error and
! reaches its exit.  The reason is the same thing that makes it
! compact: because the shift is by zero the expected values are the
! inputs, and the CTs index them through the SAME register as the
! operands, so a wrong index moves both sides together.  A loop that
! silently ran once still reaches the end.
!
! So the run_tests entry also asserts the accumulator's FINAL contents
! -- WRDA[1] in the left word, WRDB[1] in the right -- which is state
! that accumulates across iterations and which both injections do
! change.  Without those two checks this program is close to vacuous
! on the model; with them it pins that the index register stepped and
! that the loop went round twice.
!
! FRAMEWORK SUBSTITUTIONS.  CHKSZ is the routine's shared "size check"
! error path (it eventually reaches the PE2NA/PE2NB/PE2P exits on
! p.198); here it is a halt at its own address.  The block's tail --
! SIC,SENO+.32 / B,SSW -- is the SSIP return and becomes PASS.

! -- SSIP framework substitutes --
        SLC, (8)23733.0
CHKSZ   BEW, $

! -- index control word and data tables (p.199) --
        SLC, (8)24117.0
XA      XW, 0, 2, XA                 ! VALUE 0, COUNT 2, REFILL itself
WRDA    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000125252525252525252
        DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000052525252525252525
WRDB    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1252525252525250000000
        DD(BU,64,8), (8)0525252525252524000000

        SLC, (8)22367.0
SAP25   LX, $X1, XA
SHF0    L(BU,64), WRDA($X1), 64
        +(BU,64), WRDB($X1), 0
        SHF(U), 0
        CT0110(BU,52), WRDA+.12($X1), 64     ! zero shift, high 52 bits
        BZB, $RZ, CHKSZ
        CT0110(BU,44), WRDB($X1), 20         ! zero shift, low 44 bits
        BZB, $RZ, CHKSZ
        CBR+, $X1, SHF0
        B, $+1.
        B, SHF0
PASS    BEW, $
        END, SAP25
